* x1 = 4*x1b2 + 2*x1b1 + 1*x1b0
* order literals: x1ge{v} means x1 >= v, channelled to the bits both ways.
* these are the big-M forms of what the solver, which came later,
* writes with veripb's arrow syntax as
*     x1ge{v} ==> 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= v      (_up)
*     x1ge{v} <== 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 >= v      (_dn)
@x1ge1_up 4 x1b2 2 x1b1 1 x1b0 1 ~x1ge1 >= 1 ;
@x1ge1_dn 4 ~x1b2 2 ~x1b1 1 ~x1b0 7 x1ge1 >= 7 ;
